Component whose licence declaration is being fixed

  @gpustack/core-ui — the shared component library this console imports in 419
  files (see package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml).

  State: the version this console resolves declares no licence. Its package
  manifest has no `license` field, the registry therefore reports the package as
  `Proprietary` — npm's label for "no grant stated" — and the repository it is
  built from carried no LICENSE file. A grant that is not stated is not a grant,
  so the artifact a recipient downloads does not say what terms it comes under.

  The fix is prepared, not published: that repository now carries the
  Apache-2.0 text and a `license` field, and the version bump that will ship them
  is in progress. Neither is in 1.1.20 — checked by reading the published
  metadata, and by listing the tarball: it contains no LICENSE file at all. Until
  a release carries it and this console is moved to that release, the paragraph
  above describes what the shipped bundle actually contains, which is why it
  stays here rather than being deleted early.

  The component is also a branding surface this repository cannot rebrand from
  here: it exports ready-made text and image references (for example
  `AddWorkerDockerNotes`, consumed as data in
  src/pages/cluster-management/components/), and it carries a Footer component
  that links to https://gpustack.ai. That Footer is not rendered by this console
  today — the console has its own — but it is present for whoever adopts it next.

For an authoritative, machine-generated inventory of the components actually
shipped in a given build, generate an SBOM and a license report from the
installed tree rather than relying on the lists above:

    pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
    npx --yes sbom-tool generate -b . -bc . -pn OriginHub-Console -pv 0.0.0 \
        -nsb https://originhub.local -o ./_sbom
    npx --yes license-checker --production --summary
